Schwarzerblitz will be part of the IndieBreakdown tournament on the [b]12th December, 2020, 20:00 UTC[/b]! Here's what you need to know:
[list]
[*] The tournament will be played using the Steam version of the game, set in Tournament mode (options > game options > tourney mode). This mode contains only the stages and characters that are tournament legal;
[*] Tournament open to [b]EU/NA/SA[/b] due to network reasons;
[*] All matches will be played through [url=https://parsecgaming.com/]Parsec [/url]or Steam Remote Play;  a controller is [b]required [/b]to ensure maximum compatibility. [b]PLEASE [/b]be sure to test your setup before the day of the event;
[*] You will be required to join both the Schwarzerblitz Discord Server (link in the game's main menu or [url= https://discord.gg/vXKrvpV]here[/url]) and the [url= https://discord.gg/d8URTA4]IndieBreakdown Discord server[/url];
[*] Sign-up link on [url=https://smash.gg/tournament/indie-breakdown-winter-2020/details]smash.gg[/url]
[/list]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/37436603/0aed21783c9ae004a3dfe02959efc08e1c93b165.png[/img]

[h1][b]Schwarzerblitz v 1.2.3 (13.06.2020)[/b][/h1]

[b]NOTE:[/b] The following changes apply only to Tournament Mode. No change applies to the normal version of the game.

[h2]System changes[/h2]
[list]
[*] removed "demo matches" from Tourney Mode;
[*] removed "vs AI" match types from Tourney Mode;
[*] replaced stage "Containment Breach" with a version without light effects for tourney use;
[*] removed stage "Elevator" from Tourney Mode;
[/list]
